<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
<title>VQMetrix — See the quality behind your bitrate.</title>
<meta name="description" content="A video quality workbench for HaishinKit. Measure VMAF on macOS, compare encoding settings, and bring device samples into one history.">
<meta name="theme-color" content="#101318">
<link rel="icon" href="/VQMetrix/assets/app-icon.png">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/VQMetrix/assets/site.css">
<link rel="alternate" hreflang="en" href="https://haishinkit.github.io/VQMetrix/">
</head>
<body>
<a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
<header class="wrap"><a class="brand" href="<%= home %>"><img src="/VQMetrix/assets/app-icon.png" width="36" height="36" alt="">VQMetrix</a><nav aria-label="Main navigation"><a href="#workflow">Workflow</a><a href="<%= guide %>">Docs</a><a href="https://github.com/HaishinKit/VQMetrix">GitHub</a></nav></header>
<main id="main">
<section class="hero wrap">
<p class="eyebrow">HAISHINKIT / VIDEO QUALITY WORKBENCH</p>
<h1>See the quality<br>behind your bitrate.</h1>
<p class="intro">Find the encoding settings that work for your video. Compare VMAF, inspect the trade-offs, and keep every experiment in view.</p>
<div class="actions"><a class="button primary" href="https://github.com/HaishinKit/VQMetrix/releases/tag/<%= version %>">Download for macOS</a><a class="button" href="<%= guide %>">Understand VMAF</a></div>
<a class="text-link" href="#first-launch">First-launch help</a><p class="requirements"><%= version %> · Apple Silicon · macOS 26.0+ · Free & open source</p>
<figure class="app-shot"><img src="/VQMetrix/assets/macos-measurement.png" width="<%= screenshot_width %>" height="<%= screenshot_height %>" alt="VQMetrix macOS app showing a video preview and measured VMAF results"><figcaption>VQMetrix 1.3.0: a four-frame 640×360 test sample evaluated with VMAF v1. The app offers v1 and v0.6.1; scores are specific to this run.</figcaption></figure>
</section>
<section class="wrap section" id="bitrate-search"><h2>Find a bitrate for your quality target</h2><p>Set an arbitrary mean VMAF target and bitrate range. VQMetrix replays a fixed sample, narrows the candidates, and confirms the estimate in a separate trial. Keep every completed attempt in History and HTML reports.</p><figure class="app-shot"><img src="/VQMetrix/assets/macos-bitrate-search.png" width="<%= search_width %>" height="<%= search_height %>" loading="lazy" alt="Saved bitrate search with target mean VMAF 92.5 and all trial results"><figcaption>This sample confirmed 0.500 Mbps at mean VMAF 94.31. The trial limit was reached before the requested precision. An estimate is sample-specific, not a guaranteed global minimum or live-network recommendation.</figcaption></figure><a class="text-link" href="<%= documentation_base %>/bitratesearch/">Read the bitrate search guide</a></section>
<section class="wrap section" id="first-launch">
<details><summary>macOS blocked the first launch?</summary>
<p>VQMetrix is ad hoc signed and not notarized by Apple. If you trust the download from this GitHub repository:</p>
<ol><li>Extract the ZIP, move VQMetrix to Applications, and try opening it once.</li><li>In System Settings → Privacy & Security, select Open Anyway for VQMetrix.</li><li>Confirm Open and authenticate if prompted.</li></ol>
<p><a class="text-link" href="https://support.apple.com/en-us/102445">Apple’s official instructions</a></p><p class="fine">Do not disable Gatekeeper globally. Malware-detected or damaged-app warnings are different issues.</p>
</details></section>
<section class="wrap section" id="workflow">
<div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">A SHORTER EXPERIMENT LOOP</p><h2>Capture. Compare. Refine.</h2><p>Keep quality decisions connected to the material and settings that produced them.</p></div>
<div class="steps"><article><span class="label">CAPTURE</span><h3>Start with your video</h3><p>Measure on the Mac, or save camera and screen-composition samples in the HaishinKit Android Example. Create reference video and bitrate variants.</p></article><article><span class="label">COMPARE</span><h3>Make the trade-offs visible</h3><p>Compare H.264 and HEVC settings with VMAF. Uploaded Android samples can include replay latency, speed, app CPU, memory, and thermal state.</p></article><article><span class="label">REFINE</span><h3>Keep the evidence</h3><p>Return to saved runs, compare settings, and export HTML reports to share the results behind your choices.</p></article></div>
</section>
<section class="transfer wrap section"><div><p class="eyebrow">DEVICE → MAC</p><h2>Your device makes the samples.<br>Your Mac does the analysis.</h2><p>Start Receive on your Mac. Find it through Bonjour on the same local network, enter the four-digit session code, and upload. Validated packages are evaluated and saved to History.</p><a class="text-link" href="<%= documentation_base %>/transfer/">Read the transfer guide</a></div><figure><img loading="lazy" src="/VQMetrix/assets/macos-receiver.png" width="<%= receiver_width %>" height="<%= receiver_height %>" alt="The VQMetrix local-network receiver screen"></figure></section>
<section class="wrap section learn"><div><p class="eyebrow">READ THE SCORE</p><h2>A number is a starting point.</h2><p>VMAF compares an encoded video with its reference. A higher score generally means closer visual quality, but content, model, resolution, and viewing conditions matter.</p><a class="text-link" href="<%= guide %>">Learn how to interpret VMAF</a></div><aside><span class="label">FOR LIVE STREAMING</span><p class="target">90<span>+</span></p><p>A practical initial mean-score target to explore, not a quality guarantee. Check difficult scenes, dropped frames, latency, and thermal stability alongside it.</p></aside></section>
<section class="wrap section resources"><h2>Built to work with HaishinKit.</h2><div class="resource-grid"><a href="https://github.com/HaishinKit/HaishinKit.kt/pull/470"><span class="label">ANDROID EXAMPLE</span><h3>Capture integration</h3><p>Camera and MediaProjection capture live in the SDK Example. APK distribution belongs to HaishinKit.kt.</p></a><a href="/VQMetrix/android/index.html"><span class="label">ANDROID TRANSFER</span><h3>A small, standalone library</h3><p>Bonjour discovery and upload, available on JitPack. Android API 26+; no HaishinKit dependency.</p></a></div><pre><code>implementation("com.github.HaishinKit:VQMetrix:1.3.0")</code></pre><p class="fine">Performance data measures offline replay and whole-app resources. An iOS capture/telemetry app is not included.</p></section>
</main>
<footer class="wrap"><div><strong>VQMetrix</strong><p>An open-source tool for better video experiments.</p></div><nav aria-label="Footer"><a href="https://github.com/HaishinKit/VQMetrix">GitHub</a><a href="<%= documentation_base %>/">DocC</a><a href="https://github.com/HaishinKit/VQMetrix/blob/main/LICENSE.md">BSD-3-Clause</a><a href="https://haishinkit.com">HaishinKit</a></nav><p class="fine">macOS builds are ad hoc signed and not notarized. Dependency license notices are included with the app.</p></footer>
</body></html>
